==French==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|fr|frm|laisser}}, from {{inh|fr|fro|lesser}}, {{m|fro|lessier}}, {{m|fro|laissier||to let, let go, leave}}, from {{inh|fr|la|laxo|laxō, laxāre|to relax, loosen}}; possibly partly from or influenced by {{der|fr|goh|lāzan||to let, let go, leave}} ({{cog|de|lassen}}), from {{der|fr|gem-pro|*lētaną||to let, leave, leave alone}}, from {{der|fr|ine-pro|*leh₁d-||to leave, let}}. Cognate with {{cog|ang|lǣtan||to allow, let go, leave, rent}}, {{cog|got|𐌻𐌴𐍄𐌰𐌽||to release, forgive}}. Conflated also with {{cog|fro|laiier||to leave, abandon, allow}} (compare {{cog|pro|laihar}}, {{m|pro|laiar}}, Old Northern {{cog|it|lagare}}), also of {{cog|gem}} origin, from {{cog|got|𐌻𐌰𐌲𐌾𐌰𐌽||to lay, let lie, leave}}, from {{der|fr|gem-pro|*lagjaną||to lay}}. More at {{l|en|let}}, {{l|en|lay}}.

